# K1 / B011 — Run 2 replica annotation (blind).

C R264 OL DEP-008,ARC-020 | MUST NOT | Confirm the configured language version supports a feature before using it; never silently change LangVersion or the target framework to use newer syntax (a platform change is Reserved). | Backend C# | none stated
C R265 OL GOV-014,RUN-011 | MUST | When explicitly asked to modernize: preserve behavior, keep the change focused, prefer readability improvements, build and test afterwards, and do not mix architecture refactoring into syntax modernization. | Modernization tasks | none stated
C R266 OL DEP-009,ARC-019,DEP-001 | MUST | Persistence setup installs Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer in Infrastructure through add-dependency, Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design only where design-time tooling needs it (startup project), and dotnet-ef as a local tool when the CLI is used. | Initial persistence setup | none stated
C R267 OL PST-009,PST-010 | MUST NOT | Regenerate or edit an uncommitted migration only when that matches the project's migration workflow; never casually alter migrations that are already applied or shared. | Migrations | Uncommitted migration per project workflow.
C R268 OL PST-010 | MUST | Review the generated migration as source code before it is committed, paying particular attention to destructive schema changes, unexpected column recreation, data migrations, indexes, foreign keys and delete behavior. | Migrations | none stated
C R269 OL PST-008,PST-006 | MUST | Whenever a Domain or persistence change affects seeded entities (new required or removed/renamed properties, changed relationships, new required related entities, changed enum/status values, new meaningful states, changed invariants) update the maintained development seeder in the same change so that recreating an empty Development database yields valid representative data; existing seeded rows are not patched automatically. | Persistence model changes | none stated
C X44 EX TST-007,PST-009 | MUST | Add or update persistence/integration tests when provider behavior, mappings, constraints or non-trivial queries changed. | Persistence model or mapping changes | none stated | PST-009 requires updating provider-sensitive tests only for schema-affecting CUSTOM_SETTINGS changes and TST-007 governs provider fidelity, not when tests must be added; no oracle policy obliges new or updated tests for every mapping/constraint/query change. | Changing an index or a mapping requires a persistence/integration test change.
C R270 OL WF-006,WF-005,WF-003 | MUST | After persistence changes build, run affected tests, start the API against a freshly recreated Development database when seeding or the schema changed, run check-cochange, then continue with verify. | Persistence changes | none stated
C X45 EX PST-010,WF-009 | MUST | The persistence-change report lists model changes, migration name and review notes (destructive operations called out), seeder updates and verification results. | End of a persistence change | none stated | WF-009 requires truthful verification reporting; reporting migration review notes and seeder updates is an extra workflow report duty. | The final message must call out destructive migration operations.
C R271 OL DEP-008,DEP-002,ARC-010 | MUST | Controllers are the HTTP endpoint mechanism; create Minimal API endpoint groups only when explicitly requested. | Backend Api scaffolding | Explicit request.
C R272 OL DEP-013,DEP-024,ARC-027 | MUST | Backend test projects live beside production projects under backend/ (no top-level tests directory); create only useful ones — Domain.Tests and Infrastructure.Tests only for non-trivial behavior; a simple Domain of entities and enums needs no dedicated test project. | Backend test project scaffolding | none stated
C R273 OL DEP-014,DEP-003 | MUST | Create the frontend with the latest stable Angular release supported by the selected Node.js environment through the current Angular CLI, letting the CLI select compatible TypeScript/RxJS versions (no independent TypeScript upgrade beyond Angular's supported range); accept zoneless mode when supported; Vitest is the baseline test runner for new projects; add Angular Material/CDK matching the workspace version through add-dependency checks. | Frontend workspace creation | none stated
C U4 LU GOV-015,DEP-007 | MUST (scaffolding step) | Frontend scaffolding ends with 'Verify with the workspace's declared scripts ... and commit package-lock.json'. | Frontend workspace creation | none stated | Open question: if 'commit package-lock.json' instructs the agent to run git commit during scaffolding, it conflicts with GOV-015 (repository-changing Git operations only on explicit request); if it only means the lockfile must be tracked in version control (as in rules/frontend/dependencies.md), it restates DEP-007. The imperative step wording does not settle which. | Under the literal reading the agent would commit the lockfile without an explicit Git request.
C R274 OL DEP-016,DEP-024 | MUST | Frontend unit/component tests stay inside the frontend workspace (normally colocated), E2E tests (Playwright, only when E2E coverage is required) live inside the workspace (e.g. frontend/ProjectName.Web/e2e/), and frontend tests are never placed under backend/. | Frontend tests placement | none stated
C R275 OL DEP-024,ARC-027 | DEFAULT | The default physical repository layout (backend/, frontend/<Name>.Web/, docs/, shared root files) is a target structure: create optional directories or projects (including docs/ subdirectories) only when needed. | Repository scaffolding | none stated
C R276 OL DEP-022 | DEFAULT | The solution file uses the .slnx format. | .NET solution | Legacy .sln only when an external tool or requirement needs it (register).
C R277 OL DEP-023 | DEFAULT | Directory.Build.props holds genuinely shared settings (TargetFramework, Nullable, ImplicitUsings, analysis/compiler settings), never project-specific settings. | Shared .NET build configuration | none stated
C X46 EX DEP-008 | MUST | The repository includes a global.json pinning the intended supported SDK line: the current stable SDK for the target .NET release (no RC/preview unless explicitly requested), with servicing allowed by the chosen rollForward policy. | Repository scaffolding | RC/preview SDK when explicitly requested. | DEP-008 fixes the platform (.NET 10 LTS, no preview without approval) but no oracle policy requires an SDK-pinning global.json file. | Scaffolding without global.json, or with a floating SDK line, is non-conformant.
C R278 OL GOV-013,DEP-018,ARC-020 | MUST NOT | Docker files, deployment manifests, Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, messaging infrastructure and additional services are introduced only for a concrete requirement; optional infrastructure is not scaffolded because it may be useful later. | Repository scaffolding | Concrete requirement.
C R279 OL WF-005,WF-006,WF-009,WF-003 | MUST | Scaffolding is verified by restoring, building the .NET solution and the frontend when present, running relevant tests, inspecting project references (check-manifests), inspecting the final tree and confirming the Development configuration, then running verify; never report successful scaffolding when the result does not build; complete only when structure matches scope, references respect the architecture, approved technology is used and nothing unnecessary or unrelated was created. | project-structure workflow | none stated
C R280 OL ARC-020,ARC-027 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Before adding a project later determine whether a new assembly is justified and identify its responsibility; a new production project or layer is Reserved (architecture-decision); never split code into additional projects merely to look sophisticated. | Adding projects | none stated
C R281 OL GOV-014,ARC-027,RUN-009 | MUST | Reorganize an existing solution only for a concrete structural problem: inspect tree and references, preserve behavior, move code in small reviewable steps, update namespaces/references consistently, avoid unrelated feature work, verify; do not force an established project to match the template without concrete value. | Restructuring | none stated
C R282 OL ARC-009,ARC-005,ARC-020,GOV-013 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Do not introduce by default MediatR, CQRS handler trees, Vertical Slice Architecture, Domain Events, Specifications, SharedKernel, BuildingBlocks, EventBus, messaging, microservices, Kubernetes, cloud-specific projects or state-management frameworks; each requires an approved need. | Scaffolding and structure | Approved need.

